content.text:
The runtime catalog now has explicit effective values and weights, with provenance:

- authored values stay untouched;
- missing values are filled by the existing stat-based appraisal model;
- omitted weights use type-aware physical defaults, while current content already has authored weights;
- the audit exposes which entries are derived so we can later replace them with simulation-calibrated values.

I’m doing the final guardrail pass and committing this economy audit/fill layer.

Got it—you don’t want a permanent auto-pricer masquerading as authored design. I’m changing course:

- remove the silent DSL fallback;
- make omitted weight a real audit failure;
- use the scanner/model only to produce starting suggestions;
- lock those suggestions into explicit authored economy data;
- let future hand edits change the actual values directly.

That preserves the estimates as a tool, while the runtime uses authored numbers.

